hev-socks5-server for Debian
===========================

Overview
--------
hev-socks5-server is a high-performance SOCKS4/4a/5 proxy server written in C.
This Debian package provides the server binary, systemd service files, and
default configuration.

Key Features
------------
 * SOCKS5 protocol support (RFC 1928) with TCP and UDP forwarding
 * SOCKS4 and SOCKS4a protocol support
 * Username/password authentication
 * Multi-IP listener support (up to 16 addresses)
 * IPv4 and IPv6 support
 * YAML-based configuration
 * systemd integration

Configuration
-------------
The default configuration file is located at:
  /etc/hev-socks5-server.yml

A sample configuration is provided. Edit this file to configure:
  * Listen addresses and ports (supports multiple IPs)
  * Authentication settings (optional)
  * Logging and timeouts
  * UDP relay settings

Systemd Services
----------------
Two service files are provided:

hev-socks5-server.service - Standard service
  systemctl start hev-socks5-server
  systemctl enable hev-socks5-server

hev-socks5-server@.service - Instance service for multiple configs
  systemctl start hev-socks5-server@instance1
  systemctl enable hev-socks5-server@instance1

For the instance service, configuration files should be placed at:
  /etc/hev-socks5-server/instance1.yml

Authentication
--------------
To enable authentication, add to the config:

  auth:
    file: /etc/hev-socks5-server/auth.txt

The auth file format:
  username password [mark]

Example:
  user1 pass1
  user2 pass2 1a

Reload authentication without restart:
  killall -SIGUSR1 hev-socks5-server

Logging
-------
By default, logs go to stderr and are captured by systemd journal:
  journalctl -u hev-socks5-server -f

To log to a file instead, set in config:
  misc:
    log-file: /var/log/hev-socks5-server.log

Security
--------
 * Run as non-root user when possible (bind to ports > 1024)
 * Use authentication in untrusted environments
 * Limit access via firewall rules
 * Consider using socket marks for connection filtering

Documentation
-------------
Full documentation and examples:
  /usr/share/doc/hev-socks5-server/
  https://github.com/heiher/hev-socks5-server

